        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0761eca9-78e5-5db4-8b42-b448fa22633b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: That Darn Cat!, Perri, The Ugly Dachshund, The Love Bug, The Million Dollar Duck, Beethoven\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- People: Dean Jones, Felix Salten, Suzanne Pleshette\n- Characters/Roles: Jim Douglas, Albert Dooley, Dr. Herman Varnick\n- Topics: Disney live-action films\n\nFacts:\n- Perri is a 1957 film from Walt Disney Productions based on Felix Salten's 1938 work \"Perri: The Youth of a Squirrel.\"\n- Dean Jones played Jim Douglas in The Love Bug in 1968.\n- The Ugly Dachshund is a 1966 Walt Disney Productions feature film starring Dean Jones and Suzanne Pleshette about a Great Dane who believes he is a dachshund.\n- Dean Jones played Albert Dooley in The Million Dollar Duck in 1971 and received a Golden Globe nomination for that role.\n- Dean Jones played Dr. Herman Varnick in Beethoven in 1992.\n- That Darn Cat! is identified as a film title in this chunk.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
